  "explanation": "The patient has experienced two blackouts separated by at least 24 hours. According to the supplied guideline evidence (AFTD2022-BLK-COM-005), a person should not drive for 10 years following two or more blackouts of undetermined nature separated by a 24-hour period. The patient's blackout mechanism status is 'undetermined_after_investigation' and diagnosis is 'undetermined'. Although the nurse note mentions a long event-free period (9.99 years), the established restriction based on the count and separation of undetermined blackouts takes precedence as it explicitly prohibits driving for 10 years in this scenario. The absence of verified evidence confirming the specific conditional criterion (no further blackouts for 10 years) does not override the explicit prohibition found in the guideline for the current status of 'undetermined' blackouts separated by 24 hours.",
